world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto5) noble; urgency=medium

  * 18 more layouts, other scripts: Arabic (101, 102, 102 AZERTY), Kurdish
    (Central, Arabic script), Persian, Urdu, Hindi (INSCRIPT and
    Traditional), Gujarati, Kannada, Malayalam, Odia, Punjabi (Gurmukhi),
    Telugu, Khmer (NIDA), Lao, Vietnamese and Berber (Tifinagh, extended).
    60 in total. Not released.
  * The layout list no longer has an empty country list (Arabic has no
    single country): libxkbregistry rejected the whole list because of it.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000

world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto4) noble; urgency=medium

  * 20 more layouts: Irish, Luxembourgish, Portuguese (Brazil, ABNT),
    Italian (142), Hungarian (101-key), Lithuanian (IBM), Maltese (47-key),
    Finnish, Swedish and Norwegian with Sami, Guarani, Hausa, Turkmen,
    Azerbaijani (Latin and Cyrillic), Ukrainian (Enhanced), Bashkir, Tatar
    (and legacy) and Tajik. 42 in total. Not released.
  * accent-space also for Linux layouts that already type like Windows:
    Swedish, Spanish (Latin American), French (Canada), English (UK,
    extended), Romanian (standard), Northern Saami (Norway).

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 01:00:00 +0000

world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto3) noble; urgency=medium

  * New command world-keyboard-windows accent-space on|off (per user,
    optional): an accent followed by Space gives the accent, as on Windows.
    Removing the package removes the unchanged files it wrote.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000

world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto2) noble; urgency=medium

  * 18 more layouts, the ones that needed only a few keys: French, English
    (UK), Spanish, Portuguese, Portuguese (Brazil), Italian, Hungarian,
    Estonian, Lithuanian, Icelandic, Faroese, Albanian, Ukrainian, French
    (Canada, legacy), Norwegian, Danish, Finnish and Dutch. Not released.
  * Names now say "(as on Windows)": xkb-data already has layouts called
    "(Windows)" (for example Italian (Windows)), which are something else.
  * A key with characters on level 5 and up on Linux is left as on Linux.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0000

world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Prototype: German, Swiss German, Swiss French and Polish (Programmers)
    layouts that type like Windows, next to the Linux layouts. Not released.
  * Lists the layouts in xkb-data's layout list (diverted, rebuilt after
    every xkb-data change), so Cinnamon (Linux Mint) can offer them.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
